{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["Afterward he mentioned, \"And a man who commits adultery with another man's wife\" — for she was forbidden. And the sense of <b>who commits adultery with his fellow's wife</b> is like \"curses his father and mother\" — for he did an evil thing." "<b>And the adulteress.</b> If she was coerced, she is not called by this name."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "Resolved the implicit subject of הזכיר as Moses (who dictates the commandments); the Hebrew leaves the subject unexpressed."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:19.393253156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}